{"id": "EUVD-2026-102941", "enisaUuid": "661c7314-7a3c-326e-924a-350f5a88ad87", "description": "MariaDB server is a community developed fork of MySQL server. From 12.3.1 until 12.3.3 and 13.0.2, SYS_REFCURSOR handling is affected because cursor-array reallocation can leave stale references in routine contexts. A low-privileged attacker can open a large number of SYS_REFCURSORs and then fetch one to trigger a use-after-free that can enable remote code execution when combined with another vulnerability. This issue is fixed in versions 12.3.3 and 13.0.2.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T16:28:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T16:54:40", "baseScore": 9.9, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://github.com/MariaDB/server/security/advisories/GHSA-mv8g-9f7q-hprm", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/91156c3de58762196605150ab3f756fe952592d1", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/9b075b2cb53338f67e7230cc585e02d2d34514ed", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/releases/tag/mariadb-12.3.3", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/releases/tag/mariadb-13.0.2", "https://jira.mariadb.org/browse/MDEV-40396", "https://jira.mariadb.org/browse/MDEV-40639"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-85748"], "assigner": "GitHub_M", "epss": 0.55, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3a34ae29-ee46-3ab9-97f9-215815a8b76f", "product": {"name": "Server", "vendor": {"name": "Devolutions"}}, "product_version": "13.0.1, < 13.0.2"}, {"id": "b8b620b8-3881-3500-9621-83e7ae90a29d", "product": {"name": "Server", "vendor": {"name": "Devolutions"}}, "product_version": "12.3.1, < 12.3.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "367f9306-1ae0-3e2d-978d-b5276e82111c", "vendor": {"name": "MariaDB"}}], "isExploited": false}